/E (6.   Several key sections of the amended IT Act play a crucial role in protecting women from cyber exploitation. Section 66E penalizes the unauthorized capture, publication, or transmission of private images without consent, a provision particularly relevant to cases of revenge pornography and leaked personal content. Section 67 criminalizes the publication or transmission of obscene material in electronic form, addressing the growing issue of cyber pornography. Section 67A further strengthens these protections by specifically dealing with the transmission of sexually explicit content, which is critical in cases involving deepfake technology and other forms of digital abuse. Section 66C deals with identity theft, which is frequently used to create fake profiles or impersonate individuals to deceive )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
